# Auth & Middleware Policy

- Do not verify JWT in `middleware.ts` (build-time secrets can break auth).
- In middleware, only check presence of NextAuth session cookie:
  - `__Secure-next-auth.session-token` / `__Host-next-auth.session-token` / `next-auth.session-token`
- Auth-required API routes must use `getSession()` from `lib/auth.ts` and return 401 on missing session.
- Do not access `process.env` directly; use `getServerEnv()` from `lib/env.ts`.

## Example

```ts
// ✅ OK in middleware: cookie presence check only
const sessionCookie =
  request.cookies.get('__Secure-next-auth.session-token') ??
  request.cookies.get('__Host-next-auth.session-token') ??
  request.cookies.get('next-auth.session-token');
if (!sessionCookie) return NextResponse.redirect(new URL('/login', request.url));
```
